{"assets":["/statement-assets/7236f1ab5e2580926036420d8a2c65226797e0fdd228b53565234f993edf7912.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1905","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. One-X"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In this sad world full of imperfections, ugly segment trees exist."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A segment tree is a tree where each node represents a segment and has its number. A segment tree for an array of $$$n$$$ elements can be built in a recursive manner. Let's say function $$$\\operatorname{build}(v,l,r)$$$ builds the segment tree rooted in the node with number $$$v$$$ and it corresponds to the segment $$$[l,r]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now let's define $$$\\operatorname{build}(v,l,r)$$$: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If $$$l=r$$$, this node $$$v$$$ is a leaf so we stop adding more edges "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Else, we add the edges $$$(v, 2v)$$$ and $$$(v, 2v+1)$$$. Let $$$m=\\lfloor \\frac{l+r}{2} \\rfloor$$$. Then we call $$$\\operatorname{build}(2v,l,m)$$$ and $$$\\operatorname{build}(2v+1,m+1,r)$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"So, the whole tree is built by calling $$$\\operatorname{build}(1,1,n)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now Ibti will construct a segment tree for an array with $$$n$$$ elements. He wants to find the sum of $$$\\operatorname{lca}^\\dagger(S)$$$, where $$$S$$$ is a non-empty subset of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"leaves"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Notice that there are exactly $$$2^n - 1$$$ possible subsets. Since this sum can be very large, output it modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^\\dagger\\operatorname{lca}(S)$$$ is the number of the least common ancestor for the nodes that are in $$$S$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test consists of multiple test cases. The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^3$$$) — the number of test cases. The description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 10^{18}$$$) — the length of the array for which the segment tree is built."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output a single integer — the required sum modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n2\n3\n4\n5\n53278\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6\n17\n36\n69\n593324855\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/7236f1ab5e2580926036420d8a2c65226797e0fdd228b53565234f993edf7912.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's look at all subsets of leaves."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\operatorname{lca}(\\{2\\})=2$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\operatorname{lca}(\\{3\\})=3$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\operatorname{lca}(\\{2,3\\})=1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Thus, the answer is $$$2+3+1=6$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's look at all subsets of leaves."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\operatorname{lca}(\\{4\\})=4$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\operatorname{lca}(\\{5\\})=5$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\operatorname{lca}(\\{3\\})=3$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\operatorname{lca}(\\{4,5\\})=2$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\operatorname{lca}(\\{4,3\\})=1$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\operatorname{lca}(\\{5,3\\})=1$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\operatorname{lca}(\\{4,5,3\\})=1$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Thus, the answer is $$$4+5+3+2+1+1+1=17$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"1905E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1905/problem/E"}